s Helcurt, Kagura, or Silvanna. Helcurt's silence cuts off his entire skill cast window, Kagura's distance and burst bypass his durability, and Silvanna's ult locks him in a zone where his mobility is irrelevant.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[\"The enemy jungle is Fanny or Ling. Hylos cannot touch either one, and \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/heroes/hylos\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Ring of Punishment\"}],\" does not punish heroes who never stand still.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":\"The enemy has Karrie, Kimmy, Baxia, or any percent-HP damage dealer stacked on your side of the draft. Three of them together shred his HP pool faster than he can sustain.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":\"Your team has no other engage. Hylos does not start fights. He survives them. If nobody on your team can initiate, Hylos games devolve into 45 minutes of poke you cannot respond to.\"}],\"\\n\"]}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"If you cannot name which of those conditions your current draft is in, Hylos is the wrong pick. He is not the Swiss Army knife roamer most players treat him as.\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The one thing that makes Hylos work\"]}]\n84:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"His kit is built around one unusual identity: Hylos runs on his health bar, not his mana bar. His passive \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/heroes/hylos\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Thickened Blood\"}],\" turns bonus Max HP into bonus Max Mana, and when the mana runs dry he pays for casts with HP instead. So every defensive item does double duty: it thickens the bar he tanks with and it tops up the pool that keeps Ring of Punishment running. Mana is a byproduct of building tanky, not a stat you shop for. The aura is always available, even on an empty mana bar.\"]}]\n85:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Every other tank has a tempo where they are vulnerable: mana-gated, cooldown-gated, or CC-immune-gated. Hylos does not have that tempo. If he is next to your carry, he is always producing peel. Ring of Punishment is a toggled aura that ticks attack speed slow and stacking damage amplification onto anyone standing next to him. His S1 is not a combo piece; it is a knockback interrupt on a short cooldown. His ultimate is a corridor: allies gain a large movement speed boost along it, enemies on it are slowed, and the cast point lands a brief near-freeze slow on everyone caught in it.\"}]\n86:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Reading the kit correctly: Hylos is a five-target escort, not a one-target initiator. The skill floor is low. The ceiling is in where you pathway at.\"}]\n87:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Laning: the first 4 minutes\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Hylos starts roam with \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/spells\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Flicker\"}],\" as the default pick and \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-1\",{\"href\":\"/spells\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Vengeance\"}],\" as the dive-heavy alternative. Level 1 take Ring of Punishment for leash damage and the attack speed debuff. Level 2 take Law and Order for the knockback.\"]}]\n89:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-2\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Leash once for your jungler, then immediately rotate to whichever carry is most immobile.\"}],\" Your first clear is not worth sitting mid. If your MM is a Lesley or Kimmy, you belong in that lane before the first wave enters tower range. Every second Hylos spends in mid lane pre-level-4 is a second your carry is farming without a zoning body.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Open level-4 ganks with Ring of Punishment toggled before you enter vision.\"}],\" The attack speed slow lands the moment you are in range, and enemies with no minimap tick catch it late. Commit S1 only after they burn their dash. Law and Order is the commit, not the opener.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Turtle at 2:00 belongs to you, not the jungler.\"}],\" Ring of Punishment plus Hylos's native HP pool means he out-sustains turtle aggro for the final stretch while your jungler smites. Stand on the turtle, not behind it. The bonus: your jungler rotates freely because you are the one holding the pit.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The power spike you are farming toward\"]}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/items/cursed-helmet\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Cursed Helmet\"}],\" plus \",[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-1\",{\"href\":\"/items/dominance-ice\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Dominance Ice\"}],\" at roughly 9 to 11 minutes. That is the two-item combination that turns Hylos from \\\"annoying roamer\\\" into \\\"5v1 objective holder.\\\"\"]}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Cursed Helmet's Burning Soul deals 1.2% of your Max HP per second as magic damage to nearby enemies, and its Curse passive stacks Hybrid Defense reduction onto them while you stand there. Ring of Punishment is already ticking magic damage per second plus stacking a damage amplifier on each target, so the two passives stack into a compounding aura that pulls several percent of enemy Max HP per second off anyone who refuses to disengage. Dominance Ice then punishes whoever stays close enough to trade with you: Lifebane cuts nearby enemies' Shield and HP Regen to 60% of normal and Fortress Shield stacks Hybrid Defense for each of them, on top of the attack speed slow Ring of Punishment is already applying. Marksmen who walked up confidently at 8 minutes now walk into a zone where their sustain is gutted and Ring of Punishment alone is already slowing every swing they take.\"}]\n8d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The practical effect: past 10 minutes Hylos is the only tank in the game who can 1v2 a Lord pit and live long enough for rotation. Not win the fight, but buy 15 seconds of stall against 5 people. That is the spike you are buying toward, not damage.\"}]\n8e:[\"$\",\"$La6\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n8f:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight positioning and target priority\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The reflex on Hylos is to ult into the enemy team and knock back the first hero you see. That reflex is wrong most of the time.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Your ult is a road, not a bomb.\"}],\" Cast Glorious Pathway behind your carries, not in front of them. The cast-point slow and the lingering enemy slow on the road matter, but the ally movement speed matters more. If your carry walks the full length of the pathway, they kite every melee threat for the full duration. If you dropped it on the enemy and your carry cannot reach it, you just bought the enemy team 6 seconds of disengage.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Ring of Punishment is a teamfight toggle, not a poke tool.\"}],\" The moment the fight starts, you stand on the highest-priority enemy DPS threat, not the enemy tank. Ring of Punishment's attack speed slow applied to the enemy Karrie or Beatrix is a real DPS reduction. Applied to the enemy Tigreal it is useless. Body-block the carry; let your teammates kite.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"S1 knockback saves your carry, it does not start the fight.\"}],\" The single most common Hylos mistake is opening a fight by Law and Order-ing a dashing assassin. You just spent your only interrupt. Save S1 for the Fanny re-cable window, the Hayabusa shadow return, the Ling sword-stance dash. Your S1 is the peel. Your teammates bring the kill.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Edge case: if your support is a pure-peel hero (Angela, Estes, Mathilda), you get to push pathway further forward because your carry has a second layer of peel behind you. If your support is a catch hero (Franco, Tigreal), pathway stays defensive. Those supports hand-grab for the kill, and your job is exclusively to keep the carry alive until the catch lands.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: defaults vs flex slots\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Two locked slots, four real conversations, plus boots.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Locked:\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",\"ul-0\",{\"className\":\"list-disc list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[\"$La7\",\". First tank item, every game. Wave clear plus aura stacking with Ring of Punishment is the single largest damage amplification Hylos gets in the entire build.\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$La8\",\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb4\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb5\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb6\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb7\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb8\"]\n90:[\"$\",\"$Lb9\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Hylos\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"91:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxShadow\":\"0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-3 p-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-14 h-14 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex-shrink-0 bg-surface-3\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L6b\",null,{\"src\":\"https://akmweb.youngjoygame.com/web/svnres/img/test/homepage_2_2_16_12